# 9. Chart behavior

The chart should support a truthful transition:

```text
[PBD historical series] ────────────┐
                                    ├── current/live region
                                    │
                                    ▼
                         [live observations]
```

If live data exists, append it chronologically. Do not overwrite the historical bootstrap series.

The UI should make the boundary understandable. For example:

- PBD badge on the historical section;
- optional visual boundary/label at the bootstrap cutoff;
- live values clearly represented as live.

Avoid implying that a PBD line is an actual market-price record.

### Empty/live transition

Before the first real trade:

```text
Historical price context — PBD
No live trades yet
```

After the first real trade:

```text
Historical price context — PBD
Live market activity
```

This is substantially more trustworthy than making fake trades disappear behind real ones.

