# 14. Testing strategy

The agent must test behavior, not just compilation.

## Seed tests

- deterministic output for the same version/property/date;
- different properties do not all get identical histories;
- valid price/share ranges;
- chronological ordering;
- no future timestamps beyond bootstrap cutoff;
- idempotent second run;
- bootstrap rerun cannot modify live records;
- exact 24-property manifest contract remains intact.

## API tests

- bootstrap history returns `provenance=bootstrap`;
- live trades endpoint excludes bootstrap data;
- combined endpoint preserves provenance;
- no private user/wallet data leaks;
- unauthenticated public endpoints remain read-only;
- rate limiting/CORS behavior remains green.

## UI tests

For at least one funding/funded/resale property where relevant:

- chart renders historical data;
- PBD badge is visible on initial render;
- live-empty state is truthful;
- a live trade appears only in live activity;
- bootstrap rows cannot be mistaken for executable orders;
- no horizontal overflow at Telegram's ~480px viewport;
- loading/empty/error states remain intact;
- touch targets remain compliant;
- existing native-Telegram design system is preserved.

