# 16. Execution order for a medium-level coding agent

Do **not** give the coding agent one giant "implement everything" prompt. Execute these small gates in order.

## Step R1 — Recon

Read the source-of-truth docs and map current property/market/history architecture.

**Done when:** exact files, existing models, endpoints, components, and tests are identified.

## Step R2 — Contract

Define the provenance contract and bootstrap cutoff/version using existing conventions.

**Done when:** TypeScript/API/data-model contract is explicit and does not conflict with business rules.

## Step R3 — Persistence

Implement the minimal migration/model changes needed for PBD historical observations.

**Done when:** migration applies, indexes are appropriate, live records remain untouched.

## Step R4 — Deterministic generator

Implement versioned bootstrap history generation for eligible resale properties.

**Done when:** repeated generation is byte/database-state deterministic and tested.

## Step R5 — Repository/service boundary

Expose separate bootstrap/live retrieval methods and a safe combined market-history contract.

**Done when:** unit/integration tests prove no bootstrap data enters live trade/order execution paths.

## Step R6 — Secondary-market API

Update property-market endpoints to expose provenance explicitly.

**Done when:** API responses are stable, typed, privacy-safe, and backward compatible where required.

## Step R7 — UI disclosure + chart

Implement/reuse the PBD disclosure and wire the historical chart to the provenance-aware API.

**Done when:** the chart has useful historical context and the PBD badge is immediately visible.

## Step R8 — Live activity

Keep Recent Trades strictly live. Add truthful empty-state handling and, where useful, a separate bootstrap-history section.

**Done when:** a real post-launch trade can be observed without reseeding or rewriting PBD history.

## Step R9 — Order book safety

If an order-book visualization is required, separate illustrative PBD depth from executable live orders.

**Done when:** bootstrap data cannot be submitted, matched, settled, or mistaken for live liquidity.

## Step R10 — Full verification

Run:

```text
npm run check
all relevant unit/integration tests
seed/bootstrap twice
manual/browser design review
```

**Done when:** all gates are green and the progress log records the exact verification results.

